<main>
  <section class="initiatives">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Work in Detail</span>
        <h2>Six Responses. One Spirit of Service.</h2>
        <p>Each programme is shaped by the same principle: understand the person and the family, respond with dignity, and remain present beyond the immediate need.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="initiative-list">
        <article class="initiative" id="school-education">
          <span class="initiative-mark" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <span class="initiative-year">Established 10 June 1996</span>
          <h2>School Education for Girls</h2>
          <p class="initiative-lead">No deserving girl should be denied an education merely because her family cannot afford it.</p>
          <div class="initiative-body">
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The need</span>
              <p>Girls from economically disadvantaged families, particularly those studying in government schools, were at risk of leaving education when household finances became strained.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The response</span>
              <p>Swami Vivekanand Students' Welfare Charitable Trust began by providing financial support for school education, creating continuity and confidence for students and their families.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="initiative" id="higher-education">
          <span class="initiative-mark" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <span class="initiative-year">Established 2001</span>
          <h2>Higher Education for Young Women</h2>
          <p class="initiative-lead">Support should not end at the school gate when a young woman is ready to pursue a larger ambition.</p>
          <div class="initiative-body">
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The need</span>
              <p>Students who had successfully completed school still faced financial and academic barriers when moving into college and higher education.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The response</span>
              <p>Maa Shardamani Trust was established to carry that support forward through financial and academic assistance for young women pursuing advanced study.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="initiative" id="boys-education">
          <span class="initiative-mark" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <span class="initiative-year">Established 2010</span>
          <h2>Education and Mentorship for Boys</h2>
          <p class="initiative-lead">The same families revealed another need: their sons were also leaving education early for want of resources.</p>
          <div class="initiative-body">
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The need</span>
              <p>Boys from economically disadvantaged households required both educational assistance and dependable guidance through long, demanding courses.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The response</span>
              <p>Gyanyogi Shri Nandkishore Sharda Adhyatma Kendra supports and mentors students pursuing Engineering, Medicine, Pharmacy, MBA and Chartered Accountancy, continuing guidance into their professional lives.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="initiative" id="family-support">
          <span class="initiative-mark" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <span class="initiative-year">Begun October 2020</span>
          <h2>Ration and Family Support</h2>
          <p class="initiative-lead">When livelihoods disappeared during the pandemic, educational support alone could not protect a family's stability.</p>
          <div class="initiative-body">
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The need</span>
              <p>A survey among students' families revealed widowed mothers, parents too ill to earn, and households struggling to balance rent, education and food.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The response</span>
              <p>Food assistance began with 50 families and now supports roughly 300. The process is designed to preserve dignity, with recovering households voluntarily making space for others in greater need.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="initiative" id="holistic-wellness">
          <span class="initiative-mark" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <span class="initiative-year">An ongoing practice</span>
          <h2>Yoga, Pranayama and Meditation</h2>
          <p class="initiative-lead">A person grows whole when the physical, mental, spiritual and emotional dimensions develop together.</p>
          <div class="initiative-body">
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The need</span>
              <p>Academic and material assistance are most effective when people also develop self-control, positive thinking and the steadiness to meet difficulty with clarity.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The response</span>
              <p>Yoga, Pranayama and meditation are offered as disciplines of balance and inner awareness—not as fitness alone—supporting calmness, resilience and purposeful living.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="initiative" id="sewing-centre">
          <span class="initiative-mark" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <span class="initiative-year">Established 2025</span>
          <h2>Women's Self-Reliance through Sewing</h2>
          <p class="initiative-lead">Practical skill can become a quiet source of confidence, livelihood and independence.</p>
          <div class="initiative-body">
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The need</span>
              <p>Women and girls from underprivileged families needed accessible vocational skills that could support both household income and personal self-reliance.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="detail-label">The response</span>
              <p>Vatsalyamayi Maa Basanti Ji Manihar Sewing Centre provides free training in sewing, tailoring and garment construction, building practical ability alongside self-respect.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Continue the Journey</span>
      <h2>Service Becomes Meaningful When It Meets a Real Person, at the Right Time.</h2>
      <p>Learn more about the Mission, ask about an initiative, or discover how you can take part in this continuing work.</p>
